1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,278
Think of a number

2
00:00:01,278 --> 00:00:02,685
between one and ten.

3
00:00:02,685 --> 00:00:03,228
Got it?

4
00:00:03,578 --> 00:00:04,783
Don't say it. Just

5
00:00:04,783 --> 00:00:05,412
hold it.

6
00:00:05,712 --> 00:00:06,824
You can't possibly know

7
00:00:06,824 --> 00:00:07,064
that.

8
00:00:07,364 --> 00:00:08,500
It's not too small.

9
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:09,635
Not too big. Not

10
00:00:09,635 --> 00:00:10,901
the boring middle.

11
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:12,217
It's seven.

12
00:00:12,917 --> 00:00:13,311
How?

13
00:00:13,661 --> 00:00:15,851
In 1976, two psychologists

14
00:00:15,851 --> 00:00:17,725
asked 558 people to

15
00:00:17,725 --> 00:00:19,662
pick a single digit.

16
00:00:19,912 --> 00:00:20,985
Seven won. By a

17
00:00:20,985 --> 00:00:22,220
lot. Almost three times

18
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:23,616
more often than chance.

19
00:00:23,966 --> 00:00:25,116
One and ten feel

20
00:00:25,116 --> 00:00:26,669
like edges. Five is

21
00:00:26,669 --> 00:00:28,223
the middle. Even numbers

22
00:00:28,223 --> 00:00:28,996
feel too neat.

23
00:00:29,296 --> 00:00:30,814
Seven feels random. That's

24
00:00:30,814 --> 00:00:32,879
exactly why everyone picks

25
00:00:32,879 --> 00:00:33,196
it.

26
00:00:33,596 --> 00:00:35,242
Wasn't seven? Comment your

27
00:00:35,242 --> 00:00:36,436
number. I'll wait.
